/farmland-atlas/texas/clay-county"],["ARC or PLC in Clay County","/arc-plc/texas/clay-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 12 grids in Clay County shows May to June came in under 90% of normal in 38 of the 75 years since 1951, and October to November did too. May to June is the wettest pair at 8.16 inches normal and costs least, while January to February is the driest at 3.03 inches. In 2025 the middle of the grids ran 244% of normal in March to April and 37% in January to February. Grid 16627 had its driest year in 2011 at 53%.</p>"}
